# HC-020 input and wrapper contract

## Input

- object with exactly one own field named `text`
- `text` is a nonempty, non-whitespace string
- at most 8,192 Unicode code points
- no additional fields

## Errors

- TypeError: `Provide exactly one nonempty string field named text.`
- RangeError: `Draft text exceeds 8192 Unicode code points.`
- cancel: `Evidence counting was cancelled.`

## Output

Exact fields: `evidenceSections`, `unknownSections`, `citationMarkers`, `semanticValidation`. The final field remains `not-performed`.

## Registration and lifecycle

- Tool registration: `count_workshop_evidence`
- Tool reference: `workshopEvidence`
- Participant ID: `workshop-local.evidence-counter.reader`
- Participant reference: `workshop-evidence`
- `prepareInvocation` validates input and supplies confirmation text
- `invoke` checks cancellation before calling the same analyzer
- returned Disposable objects are added to `context.subscriptions`

This contract does not claim live registration, discovery, call, confirmation, cancellation, disposal, Markdown parsing, source verification, or semantic review.
